    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • OMODA 4 Lands in Paris To Showcase Futuristic Styling, Looks Like a Discount Urus\n50,000 Showed Interest in Jaguar's Most Polarizing Car Yet, the Type 01, Many Have Never Owned a Jag\n10 photos\nPhoto: Jaguar\nJaguar has recently unveiled the production version of its most polarizing car that has ever borne the brand’s logo, and it has had to deal with backlash and praise both. The endurance is paying off. Jaguar executives have revealed that they have received 50,000 expressions of interest for the electric grand tourer, and most of them come from people who have never owned a Jaguar before.\nTwo years ago, Jaguar announced plans of rebranding and unveiled the Type 00 concept car, which was unlike anything built by the automaker before. The model attracted tons of backlash as well as sudden departures from the company of people who were supposed to orchestrate the revival.\nFormer chief designer Gerry McGovern was escorted out of his office earlier this year, after rumors about his departure had been circulated for months, but Jaguar dismissed them, saying he wasn’t going anywhere. It turns out that he was.\nFurthermore, Jaguar's CEO Adrian Mardell stepped down after having spent 35 years with the company and three years in the position. In his place came P.B. Balaji , the former Chief Financial Officer of Jaguar's parent company, Tata Motors.\nPhoto: Jaguar Nearly a year later, Jaguar is counting its blessings with a wave of new buyers and alienating its oldest loyalists, because four in five prospective customers interested in the new Type 01 have never owned a model of the brand before. The British house labels this as proof that its new strategy is a success.\n\" We've never had over 50,000 people say to us 'I'm really interested in what you’re doing. We call this KMIs (Keep me informed), so we talk to them on a regular basis ,\" Jaguar managing director Rawdon Glover revealed in a conversation with Australian publication Drive. Glover says the response has validated the automaker’s decision to move into a higher price bracket.\nWhile the electric sedan is expected to start at around 300,000 Australian dollars on the local market, Americans will be able to get one for a starting price of $130,000, following its global debut in New York earlier this month.\nFor the money, customers get the luxury GT with a tri-motor setup, pushing out 1,015 horsepower (1,030 metric horsepower) and 1,007 pound-feet (1,365 Newton meters) of torque. Those are enough to make it flash from 0 to 60 mph (0 to 97 kph) on its way to a top speed of 150 mph (241 kph).\nPhoto: Jaguar Sitting on an 850-volt architecture and equipped with a 118- kWh battery pack, the Jaguar Type 01 can drive up to 450 miles (720 kilometers) before it needs to be plugged in again, according to the WLTP rating. The EPA estimate sits at around 400 miles (644 kilometers).\nHowever, it will take a while until those interested will be able to buy the controversial Jaguar Type 01. Order books are expected to open in 2027. Deliveries are scheduled to begin in the second half of next year. The car is designed, engineered, and built in the UK, with production taking place at JLR's Solihull plant.\nJLR's sales success will entirely depend on how many of these 50,000 curious onlookers confidently transition from an email list to putting down a hard deposit. Registering on the Jaguar website required only an email address and basic data. It did not require a financial deposit or a secured build slot.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nJaguar Type 01 jaguar Jaguar EV Jaguar Type 01 price Jaguar Type 01 horsepower\nAbout the author: Elena Luchian\nElena started off as a sports reporter and five years later switched to automotive. How does that happen? Lots of writing, testdrives, traveling, off-road driving courses, track driving courses, defensive driving courses and diplomas. The diplomas might be \"useless\", but the knowledge she gained is priceless. Full profile\nUP NEXT Perseverance Rover Breaks the Record for Total Distance Driven on Another Planet",
